          "width": 250,
          "height": 395
        },
        "pageimage": "Fountains_copy.jpg",
        "extract": "The Fountains of Paradise is a 1979 science fiction novel by British writer Arthur C. Clarke. Set in the 22nd century, it describes the construction of a space elevator. This \"orbital tower\" is a giant structure rising from the ground and linking with a satellite in geostationary orbit at the height of approximately 36,000 kilometres (approx. 22,300 miles). Such a structure would be used to raise payloads to orbit without the expense of using rockets. The novel won both the  Hugo and Nebula Awards for Best Novel.",
